We'll have to bite the bullet and admit that some things are just
done better by the government? This has never been proven and
is continually being eroded as a principle.



   The principle problems of list PPLs are

a) no enforcement mechanism. giving PPL owners the ability to remove
postign access solves that
b) transaction costs for ANY PPL financial transactions are high in terms
of time taken. (e.g. send snail checks) A list currency based on the yearly
subscription fee solves this


  Solve these problems and list ppl markets have a chance. 

(when cryptoanarchy gets here,even more features of government will be
privatized because of lower "transaction time" costs and degree-of-freedom)



